        "id": 142502,
        "name": "The Burning Stickman",
        "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-06-25T15:26:03.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Nielzabub\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nielzabub/48/1986_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Nielzabub:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Trajector wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;Foote wrote:<br><blockquote>Damage reduction of 1 is fairly common, even in random groups of 3 heros. With H-2 being by far and large the average instance of damage Villains generally deal, it's a lot more common to completely nullify damage instead of just mitigating it a little bit.&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nFair enough. The first time we finally beat the Matriarch, we did it by playing with H = 2 for exactly that reason.\n</blockquote></div>\nI've defeated Matty pretty handily with four to five heroes. It depends on your team. Probably the easiest game with her invovled one where H was four. Maka got a turn one Savage Mana and ate the mask. That combined with damage prevention, everyone was in their twenties by the time that game ended.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>And with that out early, he could drop a rampage and just eat the birds.</p>\n<p>I'm now imagining Matriarch standing there looking annoyed while Haka grins with feathers in his teeth.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
